# Pandemonia Project Structure

Complements `base-godot-rules.mdc` (which owns composition, SRP, signals, naming, performance). This file owns repo-specific facts that cannot be inferred from the code.

## Stack

- Godot 4.7 stable, **3D** (Jolt physics), Forward+ renderer.
- **GDScript only.** No C#.

## Directories

- `systems/` — portable, game-agnostic building blocks. `components/` holds attachable node components.
- `src/` — the actual game. Composes systems and components into actors, worlds, and the app shell (`src/main.tscn`).
- `ui/` — the game's UI: menus, HUD.
- `sandbox/` — playground for developing and testing new features. What pans out is merged into `src/`. Never shipped.
- `assets/` — art and audio. Downloads live in `assets/third_party/`; everything else in `assets/` is first-party by convention. No scripts.

## Dependency rules (one-way)

- `systems/` depends on **nothing else** in the repo — it must lift into another project unchanged.
- `src/` and `ui/` may depend on `systems/`.
- `sandbox/` may depend on anything; **nothing** may depend on `sandbox/`.
- `assets/` contains no scripts.

## Adding a feature

Build the reusable, game-agnostic part as a component in `systems/components/`; compose it into the game under `src/`. Prototype in `sandbox/` first when unsure, then promote to `src/`.

## Style specifics

- Strict static typing on **every** variable, parameter, and return type.
- Tabs for indentation; 100 columns max (see `.gdlintrc` / `.gdformatrc`).
- `##` doc comments on classes, exported properties, and non-obvious functions.

## Commits

Conventional Commits (`type(scope): description`). Scope matches the top-level directory touched (`systems`, `src`, `ui`, `sandbox`, `assets`, `cursor`).
